                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "MagNets is an arena based game with simple problem solving. You play as bot, let's call him Mag. Since Mag has a round-head I assume he dislikes square-heads. \nGameplay Video:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ki-m9Ck9g1k\nStarting at a relaxing pace the game quickly ramps up the amount of enemies thrown at you and speed they get deployed. Gradually being introduced to new mechanics the basics always stay the same, cast your electromagnetic net (MagNet) around the square-heads and forge the parts collected into tools, preferably ones with rounded edges of course. Using these tools you then solve 'puzzles' contained within each arena and clearing them rewards progress to the next. After completing X amount of levels you will face boss fights and get introduced to characters you really don't want to destroy. :) \n\nSome of the later levels became almost tower-defense like in nature requiring a balancing act of defending structures and taking down all square-heads, which was much higher paced but controls stayed responsive. Great soundtrack, interesting side-story, loveable characters and very family friendly. Cheers.",
